WEBVTT

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.020
Let's do a little review of what's happened so far.

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:42.490
Jumping from the real Abenobashi, Sasshi and Arumi went to...

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.160
The Sword and Sorcery Shopping Arcade.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.570
The Great Milky Way Shopping Arcade.

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.370
The Hong Kong Combat Shopping Arcade.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.040
The Ancient Dinosaur Shopping Arcade.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.540
The Hard Boiled Shopping Arcade.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.800
The Exciting Campus Shopping Arcade, and from there...

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.880
...Sasshi alone went back to the Heian Era...

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.340
...then coming back, to the Fairy Tale Shopping Arcade.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.970
And finally, they went to the Battlefield Shopping Arcade.

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.790
The two are in agreement on the score that they want to go home...

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.320
...but Sasshi was told by Eutus...

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.890
...that "in the real world, Masa-jii is dead."

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:12.550
Sasshi is still keeping this fact a secret from Arumi.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.810
With my powers, we may be able to jump to a world...

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.930
...where Masa-jii's alive and well.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:32.280
No, I can make the jump. I'm sure I can!

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:33.940
I gotta believe!

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:34.970
Introduction to the Onmyou Way

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:37.800
Found it!

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.290
"Learn the Lunar Calendar." "How to Cook Giant Water Beetles."

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:45.330
"Telling Apart Mendicant Priests and Mendicant Zen Priests."

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.130
"The many-world interpretation and the Copenagen Interpretation."

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:50.920
Found it! "About Taizanfukun!"

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.230
Uh-huh, uh-huh, uh-huh! Ah, I see!

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.310
Okay!

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.070
Hey, d'you get how to do it?

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:01.970
Yeah! I didn't get anything!

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:04.750
I don't think this is written in Japanese.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.280
'Cause I don't understand what it means.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.540
Give it here for a sec.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.950
Let's see, "The Taizanfukun ceremony is a means...

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:13.690
...to generally evade networks with complex links...

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:16.790
...but with an Onmyou mystic's high potentiality and powerful hegemony...

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:21.760
...it's possible to produce a PKTDQ consolidation at a super high level...

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.800
Furthermore, the combination of geromesan is of the utmost importance...

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.270
...in order to activate the totorikirodon particles...

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:28.670
...for the PKTDQ consolidation.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.770
See? It totally makes no sense.

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:32.340
Yeah, I got most of it.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:32.990
No way!

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:34.540
It's easy.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.200
You just have to get an altar like this and a sword ready.

00:03:37.810 --> 00:03:39.610
That sounds awfully sketchy to me.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.220
What're ya talking about?!

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.450
Sketchy has always been fine when it comes to charms and things!

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.270
Sketchy is fine!

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:47.890
See? It's done.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.890
It looks pretty different...

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:51.660
Oh, just shut up!

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:54.060
It doesn't matter, just give it a try!

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.060
Being decisive is what's important in these things!

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.700
You're right...

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.220
...life's 'bout being happy-go-lucky and leaving things to chance.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.260
Scraping by day-to-day, letting the dice fall as they may.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.070
But if there's a spaceship flying by outside next time...

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:10.010
...or a dinosaur running around, or stupid girls making puppy eyes...

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:12.180
...or guns being fired, or tanks tripping along...

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.900
You better know what's gonna happen to you.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.940
Well, that's...

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:17.820
All right!

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.320
All things extant in this world...

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.220
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.700
All things extant in this world...

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:30.490
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.670
Please let us go back to where Grandpa Masa's alive and kicking...

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.670
All things extant in this world...

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:36.920
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:36.920
...and to an Shopping Arcade that's exactly the same as before.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.240
Thus shall it be.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.080
Ow...

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.600
Huh? What? Huh? Not again?!

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:20.710
Why're we naked again?!

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.580
How the hell should I know?!

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.270
Oh, I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.050
Nice night for a walk, eh?

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.930
Your clothes. Give them to me, now.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:31.970
What did you say?!

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:34.920
Well, I guess it's okay since we got our clothes back.

00:05:36.100 --> 00:05:39.380
So, we're really back in our old Abenobashi Shopping Arcade?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.750
Probably.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:52.100
I dunno, it looks pretty normal to me...

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.400
Then, were we really able to get back?

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:59.920
We've finally come home!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.960
See, Sasshi? You can do it when you put your mind to it.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.360
I've got renewed respect for ya.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:05.430
What's that?

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:06.340
I'm sending my chi.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:10.230
God, Buddha, Inari-san, Yakujin-san, I'm begging you!

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:14.090
May Masa-jii be alive and kicking!

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:20.900
Yes! He's alive!

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:21.990
I'm home!

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.780
Ah, you're home.

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:29.280
Where'd the pair of you run off to?

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.810
We were worried.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:34.760
Oh, dear.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:35.740
Huh?

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.390
What's the matter?

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:43.060
You look like pigeons popped with a peashooter.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:45.480
Oh, dear.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:47.850
What're ya saying? It's creepy!

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:51.520
Oh, is it now?

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.360
Or rather, you guys aren't colored!

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:56.730
We aren't?

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:57.530
You're not!

00:06:58.010 --> 00:06:59.560
No, we are not.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.870
It's better not to be.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.400
Do you suppose so?

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.840
Yes, it's better.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:11.250
No, it ain't!

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:14.410
Dad, I've brought the medicine.

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:17.180
Ah, THAT medicine?

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:19.480
Yes, THAT medicine.

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:23.520
Are you taking THAT medicine, too?

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:26.520
Oh, dear, please.

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:36.850
The way they talk is kinda weird.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:39.290
It gave me a tiny case of the goosebumps.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:42.820
I guess something must've happened...

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:45.650
Well, I'll be going now.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:47.530
Wait!

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.490
I didn't actually want to get into this business!

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:53.060
What I really wanted was to become a lumberjack!

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.870
What's with that? You sure changed without warning.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:58.640
Leave it!

00:07:58.640 --> 00:07:59.940
I wanted to become a lumberjack...

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:02.280
...and gallantly go off to the mountains of Canada or somewhere...

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:04.610
...to be manly and cut down trees! That was my dream!

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:09.810
In the thick forests! Larch trees! Fir trees!

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:11.880
Just look at how manly this is!

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.190
With my best gal by my side...

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.140
This is bad. He's too lively.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.090
Sasshi-san, what's going on here?

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:25.560
This still isn't the world we came from, is it? Why is that?

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:29.460
Well, maybe Masa-jii was originally born in Tokyo?

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.370
He's an Osakan, through and through!

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.640
That's strange. Well, I don't really get it...

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:36.280
...but I think I'll sorta excuse myself here or something.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:37.800
Hey! Wait!

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:41.160
You're gonna stick with me until we get back to normal for real!

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:45.170
Hey, you fucking cowboy and fucking girl there!

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.060
How're you guys doing?

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.590
On your fucking way home from school...

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:52.170
...how about buying a fucking hotdog from me, fucking Kouhei-san?

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:55.560
Oh, baby! Are you going to buy one, you fucking cowboy?!

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:57.070
All right, as a special treat...

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.500
...I'll slap on plenty of fucking ketchup and fucking mustard...

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:01.700
...on the fucking hotdogs and sell the pair of them to you...

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.130
...for a fucking 500 yen! How do you like that, baby?!

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:06.370
Thanks for your business!

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:08.710
One, two, two, three, Abeno, go!

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:09.540
Hey, there, you fucking passing by cheer girls!

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:11.260
Hot Dogs One, two, one, two, one, two, go!

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:11.260
How about having a fucking meal?!

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.520
It's Mune-mune in a cheerleader outfit!

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:18.100
It's so American, it's tres bien!

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:20.850
Oh, dievochka, dievochka, dievochka!

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.950
Yaburu, yaburu, yaburu, toruchokku, toruchokku, toruchokku!

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:25.370
In out, in out, in out!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:33.660
Excuse me...

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.400
Barf. Sasshi-kun, your father was looking for you.

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:42.010
Barf. Arumi-chan, your mother was looking for you too.

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:45.410
My dad? What could he want? Talk about unusual.

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:47.900
Why are you seriously wondering about something like that?

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:51.290
No matter what happens in this weird world, you can just leave it alone.

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.320
You're right.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:54.040
Then, for now, I'll go for the pleasure right in front of me...

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.950
One, two, two, three, Abeno, go!

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:59.820
One, two, one, two, one, two, go!

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:04.430
Sasshi, what're ya gonna do 'bout this?

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:08.700
Mune-mune's here, which proves this world's a kooky one, too.

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:10.030
Huh? What're you talking about?!

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:13.200
This looks like the real shopping arcade no matter how I look at it!

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:17.280
I understand, I'm sorry. It is my fault.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:20.880
But you know, you say it's weird...

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:24.950
...but compared to the other messed up worlds from before, this is pretty decent.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:26.350
If it's only this weird...

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.670
What's the point in compromising?!

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:29.310
There's only one real world!

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:31.290
There now, Arumi-san.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:34.570
Arumi-san, your dear father is calling for you.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.080
Arumi, your mom's calling to you.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.070
There's no way my mom'd say, "Your dear father is calling for you."

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:44.040
Come on, she's an ol' lady of Osaka.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:46.140
That's totally impossible.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:47.880
She's gotta be an alien or something.

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.540
An alien or the Thing.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:53.310
Never mind that, just hurry up and return us to our real world.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:54.820
You can do it, can't you?

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:57.010
Well, if I put my mind to it, probably...

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:59.250
Then why don't you do it right now?

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:01.320
Don't tell me you still haven't had enough fun.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.490
Are ya saying you wanna just live in the worlds you like...

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:05.320
...like some stupid kid?

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:06.680
No!

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:10.930
Sasshi...

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:16.660
It ain't like that.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:18.870
Then what is it?

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:22.340
Are ya hiding something from me?

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:23.310
Eep!

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:26.540
What is it? What's gonna happen if we go back to our own world?

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:37.890
Nothing.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:40.130
Don't avoid my eyes! Say it properly!

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.960
There's nothing! I'm not hiding anything!

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:43.160
Then...

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:45.590
Well, let's just stay here for a bit for now.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:48.030
After all, we can make the jump anytime we want.

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:50.270
Well, later.

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:58.770
Arumi sure is a difficult one.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:02.860
She says this world's weird, but it isn't all that weird.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.690
Well, it is a bit creepy, but...

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:07.810
Masa-jii's alive here.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.980
Ow! What's going on?!

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.510
Wha? This is...

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:30.570
A stage set, a stage set.

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:35.440
A super giant stage set.

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:46.660
This is bad! It's a movie! It's a movie world!

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:49.800
My wild fantasies brought us to another weird world!

00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:51.520
Could it be that time...

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:56.640
Please let us go back to where Masa-jii's alive and kicking...

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.640
All things extant in this world...

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:59.920
....gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:59.920
...and to a Shopping Arcade that's exactly the same as before.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:03.170
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth, let them be as they should be.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:03.170
...that's exactly the same as before.

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:04.590
...gods of Heaven, gods of Earth...

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:04.590
...that's exactly the same...

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:09.010
I get it. This is the result of me asking for something realistic.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:12.150
But if this world is made up of my memories...

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:14.710
...of the movies that I've watched...

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:17.810
Oh, no! Arumi! She's in danger!

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:21.280
She's probably suffering like in that scene in that movie!

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:25.420
No, no! I can't think 'bout it! Or it'll really come true!

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:27.460
Arumi is safe and alive!

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:30.290
I just know she's alive and yelling real loud right now!

00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:33.510
No!

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:40.370
Sasshi, you moron! What the hell kinda taste in movies do you have?!

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:49.720
No!

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:09.450
Call me Snake.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:21.710
No! Oh, Sasshi! Where d'you go?!

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:25.690
Officer!

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:26.490
What is it?

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:29.200
So and so, and such and such, Arumi's in big trouble!

00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:29.910
Got it!

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:34.100
Abeno Angel Three, go!

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:39.670
Now, ride me. I can't wait.

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:40.400
All right!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.610
My old war wound!

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:50.280
Oh, me, too!

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:53.650
Now's my chance...

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.250
What is this?!

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:03.410
The police have surrounded the building! Surrender quietly!

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.000
What's going on here?

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:14.030
Oh, it feels so good. Being ridden from the back is the best!

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:17.010
Aki-nee, is Arumi's place really in this direction?

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.910
Come on, hurry up, there's someone coming up behind us.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:24.740
Or rather, we're gonna collide at this rate!

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:27.350
We're colliding! It's a car jacking!

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:32.010
We gotta be in a faster car, Aki-nee!

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:33.330
Got it!

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.950
Angel One, Two, go!

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.700
Mune-mune! And Nee-chan!

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:43.170
We three Angels will help you!

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.760
This is the Abeno Angels' final mission!

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:51.930
KITT, hurry.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:53.870
Okay, Michael.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.720
Hey, you truck there?! Who the hell are you?!

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:07.710
Shoot it!

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.560
Oh, shit!

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:52.570
The more you struggle, the more those belts will tighten...

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.950
...and in the end, it will cut your body to pieces.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:00.610
That sure took a couple years off my life.

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:01.530
Arumi!

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:02.940
Sasshi!

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:04.500
Who are you?!

00:17:04.950 --> 00:17:06.460
Sensei, here!

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:14.690
It feels so good!

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:02.060
It's a twister!

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:05.330
The twister brought Jaws!

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.110
Hurry! Oxygen tanks!

00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:33.210
Son of a bitch!

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:41.140
Sasshi!

00:18:41.980 --> 00:18:46.150
Don't worry, I won't ever let this hand go.

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:48.420
Sasshi...

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:54.690
There's no point if you let the other hand go!

00:18:59.270 --> 00:19:00.820
Open your eyes.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:03.300
I'm flying.

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:05.510
Hey, we're falling!

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:06.190
Ow!

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:16.750
Arumi, let's just run away, the two of us!

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:19.290
Like Bonnie and Clyde! Thelma and Louise!

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:23.120
Cheech and Chong! Tom and Jerry! Tex and Avery!

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:25.710
Okay, okay, I understand. I don't care anymore.

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:31.700
We, the Abeno Terrorist Angels have hijacked Air Force One!

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:33.770
Be quiet! If you move, we'll kill you!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:34.770
If you talk, we'll kill you.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:36.440
No matter what you do, we'll kill you!

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:39.170
Yeah, yeah, this is just getting to feel cheap now.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:41.510
Couldn't they get some other actors for this?

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:53.740
Nebula 71, please allow me to transform!

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:59.890
Sasshi, transform immediately.

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:01.750
Transform.

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:03.320
Roger!

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.920
Ah, so this is where you were, Sasshi!

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:11.040
Hurry!

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:14.100
Tonight at 10:04pm, lightning will strike that clock tower!

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:15.940
We'll use that as our power source and...

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:19.480
Oh, not the old war wound again!

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:23.180
And, with the dimensional travel device equipped on this machine...

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.530
...you'll be able to get back to your own world.

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:29.750
It seems like this time, we might actually be able to get back to our own world.

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:31.790
Yeah, I guess so.

00:20:32.260 --> 00:20:35.130
Sasshi, Arumi, you both take care.

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:39.460
What're ya saying? I'll see you again in our own world, Grandpa.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:42.420
Masa-jii...

00:20:44.540 --> 00:20:46.060
Call me Snake.

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:18.130
Are you a concubine? Nenene and ne!

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:21.680
Are you well?

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:22.790
Welcome!

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:26.410
Mune-chan, you certainly are enthusiastic.

00:21:26.610 --> 00:21:28.010
C'mon, c'mon!

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:39.920
This last jump was pretty impressive.

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:43.100
Arumi, why're you so tough?

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:45.300
So, where are we?

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:56.540
What the heck...

00:21:57.380 --> 00:22:01.670
I guess it was just another movie plot in the end.

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:02.960
Hey.

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:09.300
Sasshi, hurry up and come home.

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:11.680
It's time for dinner.

00:23:46.120 --> 00:23:48.560
Okay, okay, okay, everyone go away. Go away.

00:23:48.560 --> 00:23:50.360
I'm doing the preview.

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:51.330
Preview, huh?

00:23:51.330 --> 00:23:53.190
Well, it seems we're not wanted here.

00:23:53.190 --> 00:23:55.130
But I want to do the preview!

00:23:55.130 --> 00:23:56.400
Mune-chan, you certainly are enthusiastic.

00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:58.590
Shoot, there's no time for the preview again.

00:23:58.670 --> 00:24:00.070
The next episode is the final one.

00:24:00.070 --> 00:24:02.140
I guess I'll have to bet it all on my last chance.

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:03.200
What are you, stupid?

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:05.370
Like hell there's going to be a preview for the final episode.

00:24:05.370 --> 00:24:06.270
What?

00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:08.710
Oh, you're right! I totally didn't think of that!

00:24:08.710 --> 00:24:10.340
Even a monkey'd notice.

00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:12.750
Oh, my goodness. Arumi-chan, what should I do?

00:24:12.750 --> 00:24:13.580
Dunno.

00:24:13.580 --> 00:24:15.350
Next time on Abenobashi...
